    {
      "id": 37,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "Holmes puso una libra"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6], "es": "sobre la mesa."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "Holmes"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "puso", "base": "put", "sense": "place"},
        {"t": [2, 3], "es": "una libra", "base": "pound", "sense": "currency", "note": "La libra es la moneda británica, como el euro en España."},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6], "es": "sobre la mesa", "base": "table", "sense": "furniture"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 38,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "«¡Le digo, hombre,"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "que no tengo bicicleta!"}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "yo"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "digo", "base": "tell", "sense": "inform"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "le, a usted"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "hombre", "base": "man", "sense": "adult"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "que"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "yo"},
        {"t": [6, 7], "es": "no tengo", "base": "have", "sense": "possess", "note": "*Haven’t* es *have not* ([[contractions]]). *Haven’t got* es habitual en inglés británico; en EE. UU. suele decirse *don’t have* ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [8, 9], "es": "una bicicleta", "base": "bicycle", "sense": "vehicle"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 39,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], "es": "Puede llevarse dos caballos"},
        {"t": [5, 6, 7], "es": "para que lo lleven"},
        {"t": [8, 9, 10], "es": "a la mansión»."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "usted"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "puede tener", "base": "have", "sense": "possess", "note": "Aquí *can* indica permiso: le ofrece usar los caballos ([[modal-verbs]])."},
        {"t": [3], "es": "dos"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "caballos", "base": "horse", "sense": "animal"},
        {"t": [5, 6], "es": "para llevar", "base": "take", "sense": "carry", "note": "*To* + verbo indica para qué sirven los caballos: llevarlo allí ([[purpose-infinitive]])."},
        {"t": [7], "es": "lo, a usted"},
        {"t": [8, 9, 10], "es": "a la mansión", "base": "hall", "sense": "house"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 40,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Nos trajo"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5], "es": "algo de comer"},
        {"t": [6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "y comimos con hambre."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "trajo", "base": "bring", "sense": "carry"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "nos, a nosotros"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "algo"},
        {"t": [4, 5], "es": "de comer", "base": "eat", "sense": "food"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [7], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [8], "es": "comimos", "base": "eat", "sense": "food"},
        {"t": [9], "es": "con hambre", "base": "hungrily", "sense": "hunger"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Por la ventana"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5], "es": "podíamos ver"},
        {"t": [6, 7], "es": "las cuadras"},
        {"t": [8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13], "es": "detrás de la posada."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "a través de la ventana", "base": "window", "sense": "opening"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [4, 5], "es": "podíamos ver", "base": "see", "sense": "sight", "note": "*Could* es el pasado de *can*: aquí indica que podían ver las cuadras ([[modal-verbs]])."},
        {"t": [6, 7], "es": "las cuadras", "base": "stable", "sense": "building"},
        {"t": [8, 9, 10], "es": "en la parte de atrás", "base": "back", "sense": "rear"},
        {"t": [11, 12, 13], "es": "de la posada", "base": "inn", "sense": "lodging"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "En un momento dado,"},
        {"t": [1, 2, 3], "es": "Holmes se levantó"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6, 7, 8], "es": "y dio una vuelta por la habitación;"},
        {"t": [9, 10], "es": "después se quedó de pie,"},
        {"t": [11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18], "es": "mirando las cuadras por la ventana."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "una vez", "base": "once", "sense": "one-time"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "Holmes"},
        {"t": [2, 3], "es": "se levantó", "base": "get up", "sense": "rise", "note": "*Get up* también es levantarse de una silla, no solo de la cama ([[phrasal-verbs]])."},
        {"t": [4], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "anduvo", "base": "walk", "sense": "move"},
        {"t": [6, 7, 8], "es": "por la habitación", "base": "room", "sense": "building", "note": "Aquí *round* indica moverse por un lugar. Es habitual en inglés británico; en EE. UU. se prefiere *around* ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [9], "es": "después", "base": "then", "sense": "next"},
        {"t": [10], "es": "se quedó de pie", "base": "stand", "sense": "upright"},
        {"t": [11, 16], "es": "mirando", "base": "look at", "sense": "watch", "note": "*Look at* indica qué miras. Aquí *out of the window* se coloca entre *look* y *at*."},
        {"t": [12, 13, 14, 15], "es": "hacia fuera por la ventana", "base": "window", "sense": "opening"},
        {"t": [17, 18], "es": "las cuadras", "base": "stable", "sense": "building"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "Sorprendentemente,"},
        {"t": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], "es": "ahora tenía el pie muchísimo mejor."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "sorprendentemente", "base": "surprisingly", "sense": "unexpected"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "su pie", "base": "foot", "sense": "body", "note": "El inglés usa posesivo con las partes del cuerpo: *his foot*, «su pie» ([[body-possessive]])."},
        {"t": [3], "es": "estaba", "base": "be", "sense": "state"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "ahora", "base": "now", "sense": "present"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "muy", "base": "very", "sense": "degree"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "mucho", "base": "much", "sense": "degree", "note": "Para reforzar un comparativo se usa *much*: *much better*, «mucho mejor». *Very much* lo refuerza aún más ([[comparatives]])."},
        {"t": [7], "es": "mejor", "base": "well", "sense": "health", "note": "*Better* es el comparativo irregular de *well*: aquí habla de salud ([[comparatives]])."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 44,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "De repente se rio"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "y me miró."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "de repente", "base": "suddenly", "sense": "unexpectedly"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "se rio", "base": "laugh", "sense": "amusement"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [4, 5], "es": "miró", "base": "look at", "sense": "watch", "note": "Para decir qué miras, el inglés usa *look at*, con la preposición *at*."},
        {"t": [6], "es": "me, a mí"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 45,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "«¡Ya lo tengo!»,"},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "exclamó."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "he entendido", "base": "get", "sense": "understand", "note": "Aquí *get* significa entender: *I’ve got it!* es «¡ya lo entiendo!». *I’ve* es *I have* ([[contractions]])."},
        {"t": [2], "es": "lo"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "exclamó, gritó", "base": "cry", "sense": "shout", "note": "Cuando introduce palabras dichas en voz alta, *cry* no significa «llorar»."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 46,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "«Sí, claro,"},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "eso es."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "sí", "base": "yes", "sense": "agreement"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "por supuesto", "base": "of course", "sense": "obvious", "note": "Es una expresión fija: no habla de un «curso»."},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "eso es", "base": "that's it", "sense": "confirmation", "note": "*That’s it* confirma que algo es correcto. *That’s* es *that is* ([[contractions]])."}
      ]
    },
    {
